  "subRow": "Company, battalion two up",
  "note": "Bn Def two up laid on a reverse slope (IC s78 pp 429-431, IBB s69 pp 357-359): the forward posns on the part of the feature masked by the crest, within effective small arms range of it (MG1A3 457 m, ORBAT; IC s78 para 3 b p 430); OPs (two men to a section, from the depth Coy, with the FOO) on the topographical crest, held in strength by night (IC s78 para 3 a p 430; IBB s69 para 3 a p 358); the depth posn on the crest of the next high ground to the rear within supporting range, the anti-tank weapons there (IC s78 para 3 b p 430, para 4 b p 431); the FPF along the crest, nearer the FDLs when these are as much as 500 m behind it (IC s78 para 4 d p 431). Geometry only lays the two up layout with a crest line 300 m ahead; the terrain fit (PlanRevSlope) reads the real crest from the 30 m elevation and moves the plan behind it, or fails when there is none. Bn HQ (IBB S3 pp 22-24; p 23: placed centrally within the Bn locality, preferably behind the depth localities; a defended locality of 55 all ranks, concealed from the air, dug in, near the Bde axis with an alternative posn; laid about 500 m behind the rearmost depth / reserve Coy (the distance a decision, E). The RRs, a section of two in each rifle Coy, sited first in the forward localities with an alternative each 200-300 m back (IBB S8 pp 38-42; IC p 367).",
